From: hmos2sweet <hmos2sweet@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: return QDF status for a null CE handle

ce_send_single is a QDF_STATUS function. Returning the unrelated A_STATUS
enum fails with Clang 21's implicit-enum-enum-cast diagnostic under Werror.

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/ce/ce_main.c b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/ce/ce_main.c
--- a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/ce/ce_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/ce/ce_main.c
@@ -2133,5 +2133,5 @@
 	if (qdf_unlikely(!ce_hdl)) {
 		HIF_ERROR("%s: error CE handle is null", __func__);
-		return A_ERROR;
+		return QDF_STATUS_E_FAILURE;
 	}
 
